DOC_TEXT = """India is not just a country; it is a living civilization shaped by over 5,000 years of history, from the Indus Valley Civilization to becoming the world’s largest democracy. With more than 1.4 billion people, 22 official languages, and countless cultures, India represents unity in diversity in its truest form.

Modern cities like Mumbai and Bengaluru drive global innovation and technology, while villages still depend on agriculture, employing nearly 40% of the population. This contrast reflects a nation constantly balancing tradition and progress.

India’s strength lies in its people—their resilience and hope. The literacy rate has grown from about 18% in 1951 to over 75% today, showing steady progress. Festivals like Diwali and Holi bring people together, celebrating joy, faith, and unity across religions.

India has also made global achievements, such as the Chandrayaan-3 mission by the Indian Space Research Organisation, showcasing innovation with limited resources.

Despite challenges like inequality and rapid urbanization, India continues to grow with determination. It is not perfect, but it is deeply human—a nation of dreams, diversity, and unstoppable spirit."""
